<?php

namespace Symfony\Component\DependencyInjection;

/**
 * Generic stub for Symfony's service container.
 *
 * `ContainerInterface::get()` is declared `?object`, so without this stub PHPStan cannot
 * see what any of every container get(X::class) call site actually returns —
 * every one of them resolves to `object` and nothing downstream is checked. That would
 * make the analyser blind to precisely the code this wave rewrites.
 *
 * Every real call site in this codebase passes `X::class`; the only 8 that don't are the
 * generic wrapper methods (YesWikiController, BazarField, YesWikiMigration,
 * YesWikiPerformable, FormPropertiesService), which already declare
 * `@param class-string<T>` themselves and so type-check straight through.
 *
 * The real interface's `extends Psr\Container\ContainerInterface` is deliberately not
 * repeated here: a stub only overlays type information onto the real declaration, and
 * restating the parent makes PHPStan resolve it in the stub's own (non-autoloaded)
 * context, where it fails. Omitting it keeps the real hierarchy intact.
 *
 * Kept after ticket 08: the container itself is legitimate DI surface now (tests, base-class getService helpers), and this stub is what types every get() chain.
 */
interface ContainerInterface
{
    /**
     * @template T of object
     *
     * @param class-string<T> $id
     *
     * @return ($invalidBehavior is 1 ? T : T|null)
     */
    public function get(string $id, int $invalidBehavior = 1): ?object;
}
